  "worked_solution": "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(x-4)\\cdot (x+2)-7\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x-8-7 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-15 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-5) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $x$ are\n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=5.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
